# --- Rust ---
/target/
**/*.rs.bk
*.pdb

# --- Python ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
# The compiled extension module is a build artifact, never committed.
*.so
*.pyd
*.dylib

# --- maturin / uv ---
# uv.lock and Cargo.lock ARE committed - reproducible builds need them.
# build/ and dist/ are not.
/build/
/dist/
/wheels/

# --- mdBook ---
docs/book/

# --- Agent-tool integrations (generated skill exports) ---
# `tools/export_skills.py` writes azoth's catalog into each tool's discovery
# directory. Generated from skills.toml, so never committed.
.dsh/
.claude/skills/
.opencode/skills/
# A second checkout of this repository, made by an agent tool's worktree feature. A nested
# checkout is not part of this one - and `ruff` and `git status` both walk into it if it is
# not here, which is how it showed up as a dozen lint errors in another session's files.
.claude/worktrees/

# --- Lean ---
# `.lake` holds the compiled oleans and the packages Lake fetched, which for
# Mathlib is several gigabytes. `lake build` reproduces it from the pins in
# `lean/lake-manifest.json`, which IS committed - that is what makes the
# toolchain and the dependency revisions reproducible rather than merely
# recorded.
lean/.lake/
lean/vendor/lean-units/.lake/

# --- Java (the NeqSim oracle driver, compiled by hand, never committed) ---
#
# The 60 MB `neqsim-f0c7436.jar` the drivers compile against is built from the
# checkout at `/tmp/neqsim-check/neqsim` by `./mvnw -q -DskipTests package` and
# copied beside them; it is a local prerequisite, like the checkout itself. The
# whole recipe - the clone, the pinned commit the name encodes, the build - is in
# `AGENTS.md` under "The NeqSim oracle".
*.class
validation/neqsim/*.jar

# --- editors / OS ---
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# --- release artifacts ---
# provenance.json is generated per release and, once signed, attached to the
# release alongside the wheels - which is where a signature is useful, since a
# committed copy would be a second, unsigned, silently-stale record of the same
# thing. CI generates one per build and uploads it as an artifact for review.
/provenance.json

# --- user-supplied licensed data ---
# Your own data file, and the data files generated from it, are yours. Committing
# values that came from a standard you licensed would redistribute them, which is
# the thing the copyright rule exists to avoid - see docs/src/copyright.md. The
# committed copies under data/ must keep the placeholders, which is why the
# generated files are NOT listed here: gitignore cannot untrack a file that is
# already committed, so that rule is `tools/gen_user_data.py`'s to announce and
# yours to respect rather than something this file can do.
/azoth-data.toml

# --- local scratch ---
/tmp/
*.local.*

# The wasm package wasm-pack writes; it is built, never committed.
crates/azoth-wasm/pkg/

# The wasm module the editor imports; `npm run wasm` builds it from the crate.
/ui/src/wasm/pkg/

# --- the editor ---
# Rendered by `npm run dev` from `index.html`, and never committed: the wasm pkg above is the
# only generated thing under `ui/` that another build reads.
/ui/node_modules/
/ui/dist/
